{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvqFS88FASTGnMGUR8z8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017WkDC1KEvkt8KYiBPVrKU6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(r\"The difference-in-means (DiM) estimator, which is unbiased without interference, is systematically biased for the GATE under interference, and design-based\",\n r\"The difference-in-means (DiM) estimator, which is unbiased without interference, is systematically biased for the GATE under interference \\citep{Eckles2016Design,Ugander2013GraphCluster}, and design-based\")\nrep(r\"\\emph{accuracy is governed by the fidelity of the fitted exposure mapping to the generating mechanism}, not by\",\n r\"\\emph{accuracy is governed by the fidelity of the fitted exposure mapping to the generating mechanism} (a concern the interference literature raises under the heading of misspecified exposure mappings and interference of unknown form; \\citealp{Savje2023Misspecified,Savje2021Unknown}), not by\")\nrep(r\"interference with noisy or $k$-nearest-neighbour structure \\citep{Li2021Noise,Alzubaidi2023KNN}, and randomization tests for interference \\citep{Tiwari2024Quasi}. Our HT\",\n r\"interference with noisy or $k$-nearest-neighbour structure \\citep{Li2021Noise,Alzubaidi2023KNN}, and asymptotics for effect estimation under random-graph models of the network \\citep{Li2022RandomGraph}. Our HT\")\nrep(r\"\\paragraph{Designs for the GATE.}\",\n r\"\\paragraph{Misspecified exposure mappings.} Every exposure-mapping method, regression or design-based, relies on a mapping that summarizes how others' treatments reach a unit. \\citet{Savje2023Misspecified} treats the case where the analyst's mapping is misspecified and separates the definition of the estimand from the assumptions that make an estimator informative about it, and \\citet{Savje2021Unknown} study average-effect estimation when interference has unknown form. These works are analytical and concern effects defined through exposure contrasts; we instead measure, in a simulation grid, how far a regression GATE estimator is from the all-treated-minus-all-control contrast when its mapping does or does not match the mechanism, with the corner-extrapolation account of Section~\\ref{sec:corner} as our own heuristic.\\n\\n\\\\paragraph{Designs for the GATE.}\")\nrep(r\"\\subsection{A heuristic account of the corner extrapolation}\",\n r\"\\subsection{A heuristic account of the corner extrapolation}\\label{sec:corner}\")\nrep(r\"ignores cluster dependence under the cluster design and uses no resampling.\",\n r\"ignores cluster dependence under the cluster design and uses no resampling. Interval construction under network dependence is a research topic in its own right: variance estimators for design-based effects are given by \\citet{Aronow2013EstimatingAC}, block-bootstrap intervals accompany regression adjustment in \\citet{Han2023ModelbasedRA}, and random-graph asymptotics are studied by \\citet{Li2022RandomGraph}. We did not run any of these on the same grid, so we cannot say whether they would have restored nominal coverage.\")\nrep(r\"none with learned graph representations \\citep[e.g.,][]{Kipf2016GCN} or designs\",\n r\"none with learned graph representations or designs\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\nsed -n 195,225p claims_grounding.json; grep -n 'Section~3' paper.tex"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1792,"cache_read_input_tokens":90465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1792},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42579b58-83b8-4626-90f8-5debb8e4f391","uuid":"fd611673-961f-4ebf-9cd3-18565b180f4d","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:34:16.132Z","request_id":"req_011CgvqFRGHoKamE4WaLQsRP"}
