{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvqGGMHig88MScdTbzen","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NxyJyvboDNcgmf2c1tqBeM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nc=json.load(open('claims_grounding.json'))\nlast=c['claims'][-1]\nprint(last['claim'][:200], last['source_ids'])\nlast['citation_keys']=[k for k in last['citation_keys'] if k not in('Tiwari2024Quasi','Kipf2016GCN')]+['Savje2023Misspecified','Savje2021Unknown','Eckles2016Design','Li2022RandomGraph']\njson.dump(c,open('claims_grounding.json','w'),indent=2)\nE\nls .claude/skills/validate-paper/ .claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts 2>/dev/null; sed -n 1,60p .claude/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2174,"cache_read_input_tokens":92257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2174},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42579b58-83b8-4626-90f8-5debb8e4f391","uuid":"6e91952f-4fb9-4e03-8f7a-96ebbf925d1a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:34:22.867Z","request_id":"req_011CgvqGE9pMGtvfRsP8pNWu"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NxyJyvboDNcgmf2c1tqBeM","type":"tool_result","content":"Related-work statements on design-based estimation, designs for the GATE and regression adjustment cite only works by title/topic ['ref.s2.148c698ad34d340ffee56ed7b0870b5b6b095d04', 'ref.openalex.W2951409510', 'ref.s2.152133064de07df3715320d7f0a11ef10d503912', 'ref.s2.d5e7c6b392942c698a6bebab48bbd5aa34418e05', 'ref.openalex.W2617163372', 'ref.openalex.W4389363523', 'ref.openalex.W4399114673', 'ref.openalex.W3163172607', 'ref.openalex.W4385436618', 'ref.openalex.W4393213543', 'ref.openalex.W4387929707', 'ref.openalex.W3076545202', 'ref.openalex.W2946941545', 'ref.openalex.W4396817070', 'ref.s2.ea9867ecf151eade547f39e8addeb44fac4c4592', 'ref.s2.c4c7ae6d22243b398c36dae35d4b9fcd542591ab', 'ref.s2.f292d771a8a0627899871e35b8021ff1a3fbce4e', 'ref.openalex.W3011985574', 'ref.openalex.W4386435863', 'ref.openalex.W2796251014', 'ref.s2.8dbd27b8975684531b76a692ad084fed90335d3a', 'ref.s2.d5b4ebe42cdaafd922f70efce774cf91af3b5d7f', 'ref.s2.23e9ddc6a752b966e10c8e60b59b491fb92fedad', 'ref.openalex.W2953584959', 'ref.s2.68544f3f58f06ada5d3ac34ec2ea4decfc39b131', 'ref.openalex.W4389218130', 'ref.openalex.W2519887557']\n.claude/skills/validate-paper/:\nSKILL.md\nscripts\ntemplates\n\n.claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts:\ncompile_latex.sh\nvalidate_compile_inputs.py\nvalidate_figures.py\nvalidate_rendered_si.py\nvalidate_tex_refs.py\n---\nname: validate-paper\ndescription: Validate grounded paper artifacts and compile LaTeX PDF with strict fail-fast checks.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nRun final quality gate for the generated paper.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- After `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, and `claims_grounding.json` are written.\n- Before declaring final paper success.\n\n# What to do\n1. Validate sections and citation keys:\n```bash\npython scripts/validate_tex_refs.py \\\n  --tex paper.tex \\\n  --bib references.bib\n```\nRequire a substantive embedded Supplementary Information section after the bibliography. It must\nuse `\\\\appendix` and `\\\\section{Supplementary Information}`, contain grounded visible content plus\nat least one subsection, table, or figure, and contain no template placeholder text.\n2. Validate claim mappings, bibliography/provenance consistency, and every `@evidence[[...]]` link in the `scientific-evidence/` bundle:\n```bash\npython ../write-paper/scripts/validate_claims.py \\\n  --paper-data paper_data.json \\\n  --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib \\\n  --claims claims_grounding.json \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\nThis delegates to the `scientific-evidence` skill verifier, which classifies every `@evidence[[...]]` link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`. Any `dangling` link (or an `@evidence[[...]]` token with no `scientific-evidence/` bundle present) is a hard error and must be sent back to the paper-writing agent for repair.\n3. Validate figure manifest and figure readability budget when `figure_manifest.json` is present or `paper_strategy.json` requires figures. The canonical schema is `templates/figure_manifest.schema.json`.\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\n4. Compile:\n```bash\nbash scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n```\nThe compile script also validates that Supplementary Information is visibly rendered on a page\nafter References with substantive content. Source-only structure checks are not sufficient for\nconditional or literal LaTeX constructs.\nIt records and validates every LaTeX input, restricts BibTeX to the canonical `references.bib`,\nand removes inherited Kpathsea path overrides before compiling.\n5. Require `paper.pdf` to exist.\n6. When `paper_data.json.paper_profile == \"standalone\"`, also fail on visible paper language that leaks pipeline terms such as `eligible`, `correct and eligible`, `correctness rate`, `worker_01`, `worker_02`, `combined_score`, or similar internal wording.\n7. When the selected format or venue guidance requires real author metadata, also fail on anonymous or generic placeholder author blocks and emit soft warnings when title/abstract/introduction/conclusion lack venue-relevant framing or when the discussion drifts into unrelated application narratives.\n8. Fail hard on any missing grounding link, missing section, missing/empty/misordered Supplementary Information, unresolved citation, bibliography/provenance mismatch, figure-manifest mismatch, density-budget violation, page-limit violation for formats with enforced budgets, standalone-language violation, author-block violation required by format/venue guidance, dangling `@evidence[[...]]` link, or compile error.\n9. Treat the parent orchestrator's validation report as authoritative during repair rounds. Last-body-page fill is rendered geometric vertical occupancy computed from text and graphics bounds, not character count or word density. Do not claim that page validation passed using a character-count proxy. If the canonical validator is unavailable in the agent workspace, make the targeted repair and return control so the parent can compile and revalidate it.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42579b58-83b8-4626-90f8-5debb8e4f391","uuid":"ce241cd4-3152-44d1-94db-92efe23aeb79","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:34:22.954Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Related-work statements on design-based estimation, designs for the GATE and regression adjustment cite only works by title/topic ['ref.s2.148c698ad34d340ffee56ed7b0870b5b6b095d04', 'ref.openalex.W2951409510', 'ref.s2.152133064de07df3715320d7f0a11ef10d503912', 'ref.s2.d5e7c6b392942c698a6bebab48bbd5aa34418e05', 'ref.openalex.W2617163372', 'ref.openalex.W4389363523', 'ref.openalex.W4399114673', 'ref.openalex.W3163172607', 'ref.openalex.W4385436618', 'ref.openalex.W4393213543', 'ref.openalex.W4387929707', 'ref.openalex.W3076545202', 'ref.openalex.W2946941545', 'ref.openalex.W439