{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvqKbJPYt6ENEngcJoAK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fr6HapifDvAcMJh4w4YHai","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a[:50]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(r\"Every exposure-mapping method, regression or design-based, relies on a mapping that summarizes how others' treatments reach a unit. \\citet{Savje2023Misspecified} treats the case where the analyst's mapping is misspecified and separates the definition of the estimand from the assumptions that make an estimator informative about it, and \\citet{Savje2021Unknown} study average-effect estimation when interference has unknown form. These works are analytical and concern effects defined through exposure contrasts; we instead measure, in a simulation grid, how far a regression GATE estimator is from the all-treated-minus-all-control contrast when its mapping does or does not match the mechanism, with the corner-extrapolation account of Section~\\ref{sec:corner} as our own heuristic.\",\n r\"\\citet{Savje2023Misspecified} treats a misspecified analyst mapping and separates the estimand's definition from the assumptions that make an estimator informative about it; \\citet{Savje2021Unknown} study average-effect estimation under interference of unknown form. These works are analytical; we instead measure in a simulation grid how far a regression GATE estimator lands from the all-treated-minus-all-control contrast when its mapping does or does not match the mechanism, and offer the corner-extrapolation account of Section~\\ref{sec:corner} as a heuristic.\")\nrep(r\" Interval construction under network dependence is a research topic in its own right: variance estimators for design-based effects are given by \\citet{Aronow2013EstimatingAC}, block-bootstrap intervals accompany regression adjustment in \\citet{Han2023ModelbasedRA}, and random-graph asymptotics are studied by \\citet{Li2022RandomGraph}. We did not run any of these on the same grid, so we cannot say whether they would have restored nominal coverage.\",\n r\" Variance estimators for design-based effects \\citep{Aronow2013EstimatingAC}, block-bootstrap intervals for regression adjustment \\citep{Han2023ModelbasedRA} and random-graph asymptotics \\citep{Li2022RandomGraph} address network dependence; we did not run them on this grid, so we cannot say whether they would restore nominal coverage.\")\nrep(r\" The oracle's plane mean of 0.045 is similar to the per-case errors in cases 1--5, which suggests that the residual error there is mostly sampling noise at $n=3000$, but this comparison is between a per-case value and a plane mean.\",\n r\" The oracle's plane mean of 0.045 is similar to the per-case errors in cases 1--5, suggesting residual sampling noise at $n=3000$, though this compares a plane mean with per-case values.\")\nrep(r\" Practically, the results suggest allocating effort to the exposure mapping, for instance with model comparison among a small family, before investing in the graph or the design. At the same time, a gate of this kind has costs:\",\n r\" Practically, the results suggest spending effort on the exposure mapping, for instance by model comparison among a small family. A gate of this kind has costs:\")\nrep(r\" Because the per-case bias is not recorded, we can say that a substantial systematic component exists on average, not that it is concentrated in the failing cases; the model-selection plane suggests this (selected estimator: bias 0.092, RMSE 0.140) but is a separate plane.\",\n r\" Per-case bias is not recorded, so a substantial systematic component exists on average but is not shown to be concentrated in the failing cases; the model-selection plane suggests it (bias 0.092, RMSE 0.140) but is a separate plane.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\ncp paper.tex $TMPDIR/b/; cd $TMPDIR/b; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\nopen('paper2.tex','w').write(s.replace(\"\\\\clearpage\\n\\\\bibliography{references}\",\"\\\\label{endbody}\\\\clearpage\\n\\\\bibliography{references}\",1))\nE\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper2.tex >/dev/null; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper2.tex >/dev/null; grep endbody paper2.aux; PYTHONPATH=$TMPDIR/pylib python3 -c \"\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\nr=PdfReader('paper2.pdf');t=r.pages[8].extract_text();print(t[-600:])\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":100028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1000},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42579b58-83b8-4626-90f8-5debb8e4f391","uuid":"b0c600e5-38c1-49c3-a45a-48d5d12bd9bc","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:35:12.650Z","request_id":"req_011CgvqKaT3tcGSdqpiEX9oV"}
